{"id": "EUVD-2026-103723", "enisaUuid": "9cce7871-859d-3c74-bfe2-efc91d4f0be9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfc: fix use-after-free in nfc_get_local_general_bytes\n\nCommit 6709d4b7bc2e (\"net: nfc: Fix use-after-free caused by\nnfc_llcp_find_local\") attempted to fix a use-after-free (UAF) issue by\ninvoking nfc_llcp_local_put(local) after accessing local->gb. However,\nif the reference count drops to zero, local is freed immediately,\nleading to a use-after-free when callers access the returned pointer.\nAlternative approaches using dynamic allocation (e.g. kmemdup) introduced\nmemory leaks because callers consistently treat the returned pointer as\nborrowed memory.\n\nFix this properly by refactoring nfc_llcp_general_bytes() and\nnfc_get_local_general_bytes() to accept a caller-provided output buffer\n(out_gb) and its maximum length (gb_max_len). The general bytes are\nsafely copied into out_gb before calling nfc_llcp_local_put(local),\nensuring safe lifetime management without ownership transfer complications.\n\nUpdate all callers across drivers (microread, pn533, pn544, st21nfca,\ndigital_dep, and nci) to provide their own destination buffers and pass\nthem to nfc_get_local_general_bytes().", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/25bfa673adc70189c0bc872940421ae59f789cf6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b31d0cc95856c856ada91f943fb14dfdf29a923", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c40f61a6a413f3eaf028e5fe367fd9749e503ab0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/19bcfc2a56d0b82919079b5424c5a9a0ac897dcf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8c929e9afdbc33b1876ecb97a517e850449b5bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/841af260ff477f6191872bc3b2e15488615c1827", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9ede11e12f965ace97c4e0f606667f24fb41e7e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dcab71a7011918f6fdba7adcec02d217dcb84b8d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qhvx-2qrr-cpv7", "CVE-2026-98483"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04cd0804-813b-3549-8762-2cdf19f64e85", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "1b7366a7-c496-35da-b275-8b921d24e72e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b3ad46e155a6d91b36c6e892019a43e3ef3c696d"}, {"id": "248e86fb-03b2-3737-889a-9e0e227b37e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "425d9d3a92df7d96b3cfb7ee5c240293a21cbde3 <c40f61a6a413f3eaf028e5fe367fd9749e503ab0"}, {"id": "276ba81a-d4c5-3352-89c1-11ae7eb67e37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2f4b8586-f614-3e86-867a-3b321080bbc3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fc8429f8d86801f092fbfbd257c3af821ac0dcd3 <2b31d0cc95856c856ada91f943fb14dfdf29a923"}, {"id": "3409258c-f09b-3a96-bc53-9f5571c5ef17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6709d4b7bc2e079241fdef15d1160581c5261c10 <841af260ff477f6191872bc3b2e15488615c1827"}, {"id": "434e12cf-3e5d-3a31-bc6a-2abfd8f4c4db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "44dfb1af-b471-36f6-bfbe-8833a9410709", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.188 <5.10.271"}, {"id": "4a7566ad-9aeb-3e30-b058-3aaf0c55dab8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "dd6ff3f3862709ab1a12566e73b9d6a9b8f6e548"}, {"id": "649ea94c-8f97-354f-98b0-1daeccf3addd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6709d4b7bc2e079241fdef15d1160581c5261c10 <9ede11e12f965ace97c4e0f606667f24fb41e7e1"}, {"id": "686f3bdc-ffd3-3c40-93e9-e45c27426ed9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.4.4 <6.5"